    "abstract": "Illustrated parts figure for the passenger oxygen distribution manifold and the associated service unit hardware, showing the fifteen minute and the twenty-two minute generator standards.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure identifies the passenger oxygen distribution manifold accumulator, the inlet filter and the mounting hardware behind the passenger service units in the cabin ceiling, and states the generator duration rating each manifold item belongs to.",
      "figure_note": "The figure covers one cabin zone; the layout repeats along the cabin with the item quantities scaled to the seat count. The accumulator and the filter must be at the same duration rating as the generator cores fitted in that cabin, and the rating is now carried in the nomenclature of both items rather than only in their modification effectivity, because an effectivity line is easy to read past when the manifold work is planned separately from the core change. Generators of different durations must not be installed in one cabin. Item quantities on this sheet are for a 180 seat single class layout."
    },
